+# Backing Up Your App
+
+Backups protect your data. Run them before you change anything important.
+
+## Why Volume-Level Backups Win
+
+In-app exports miss hidden state. They skip uploads, queued jobs, and session
+data stored outside the database. They also depend on the app running. If the
+app is broken, so is your export.
+
+Volume-level backups capture the whole data directory. They include the
+database files, uploaded files, and configuration. Nothing is skipped. Restore
+is a copy, not a re-import, so it is faster and less error-prone.
+
+Use in-app exports when you need a portable, human-readable snapshot. Use
+volume backups for recovery.
+
+## Weekly Schedule
+
+Back up every week. Do it at the same time so it becomes routine. A Sunday
+night cron job works well.
+
+Keep three rotations:
+
+- Daily snapshots, retained for 7 days.
+- Weekly snapshots, retained for 8 weeks.
+- Monthly snapshots, retained for 12 months.
+
+Store one copy off-site. A second machine or object storage guards against a
+single server failure.
+
+## Restore Drill
+
+A backup you have not tested is a guess. Run a drill every month.
+
+1. Copy the backup to a fresh machine or empty directory.
+2. Start the app against the copied data.
+3. Check that recent records exist and uploads open.
+
+Log the result. If the drill fails, fix the backup process before you need it.
